--
-- LICENCE: THIS FILE IS UNDER THE GNU GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE 3.0 (COPYING), not the LGPL like the rest of whip_core.
-- Many of its emotes, their commands and their prop placements come from RPEmotes (GPL 3.0) by TayMcKenzieNZ,
-- Mathu_lmn, MadsL and the RPEmotes community, which grew from DullPear's dpemotes (github.com/andristum/dpemotes).
-- RPEmotes' first repository (github.com/TayMcKenzieNZ/rpemotes) is gone; it carries on as rpemotes-reborn
-- (github.com/alberttheprince/rpemotes-reborn). Any copy of this file, or anything made from it,
-- keeps these credits and stays open source under the GPL. It names only the game's own animations and props: none
-- of RPEmotes' custom ones.
--
-- Every name in here must exist in the game. Before changing this file, run the checker:
--     lua whip_core/dev/emotecheck.lua <folder with DurtyFree's dumps>
-- It lists anything that is misspelled or missing (see the top of that file for the dumps).
--
-- AN EMOTE is:
--   cmd       what players type: /e drink. Lowercase letters, digits and _ only; "c" and "place" are taken.
--   label     what the menu shows
--   category  one of the category keys below
--   and ONE of:
--     dict, anim   the GTA animation dictionary and the clip inside it, with:
--                    loop    true: keeps playing until stopped. Left out: plays once
--                    move    true: upper body only, so the player can walk while it plays
--                    freeze  true: stops on the last frame and holds the pose
--     scenario     a GTA scenario name (it brings its own props and loop)
--     props only   nothing to play: something held or worn while the player moves as normal
--   props     up to 2 things held or worn:
--             { model = 'prop name', bone = bone id, offset = { x, y, z }, rot = { x, y, z } }
--   video     optional: its preview in the menu, a file under whip_media_previews/video/emotes/ ('Emotes/wave.webm')
--
-- A WALK is { cmd, label, clipset, video }.  A MOOD (facial expression) is { cmd, label, anim }.
--
-- Two-player emotes and exit animations are not in it yet. wait12 plays 'idle' (the only clip its
-- dictionary has); backpack, brief2, papers, rose2, rose3 and shit2 are props only.

